. * nwlsm tutorial 2: how many latent clusters? BIC for the Lazega lawyers
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the package nwlsm. The data (Lazega 2001) are
>  loaded from the nwcommands website.
. set linesize 80

. 
. nwwebuse lazega, nwclear

. nwsummarize lazega_fr
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  lazega_fr
   Network id:  3
   Directed: true
   Valued: false
   Two-mode: false
   Nodes: 71
   Selfloop: false
   Arcs: 575
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  1
   Density:  .116
   Mean outdegree:  8.10
   Temporal: false

. 
. * --- one model without clusters, and its BIC ---
. nwlsm lazega_fr, dim(2) seed(12)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Latent space model (Euclidean distance; bernoulli family), posterior by MCMC
Network: lazega_fr (71 actors, directed)           Latent dimensions: 2
Draws: 4000  burn-in: 10000  interval: 10          Seed: 12
Posterior mean log likelihood: -1551.040 (sd  9.291)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                              Mean        Sd   MC s.e.  Lower 95% Upper 95%
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
_cons                       0.0175    0.1001    0.0040    -0.1770    0.2132
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Variance parameters (posterior):
sigma2                      2.4328    0.3410    0.0096     1.8340    3.1707
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acceptance rate of the latent positions: 0.239
Positions: minimum Kullback-Leibler estimate e(Z) (also estat positions); mean
of the draws aligned to it e(Zmean); posterior mean distances e(D); posterior
mean tie probabilities e(P). Positions are identified up to rotation,
reflection and translation only.

. estat bic

BIC of the latent position model (as latentnet's bic.ergmm)
--------------------------------------------
Component                                BIC
--------------------------------------------
Ties given positions (Y)            3016.530
Positions (Z)                        450.588
--------------------------------------------
Overall                             3467.118
--------------------------------------------
Latent clusters: 0; coefficients: 1; effective number of observations (ties): 57
> 5
Smaller is better. The BIC compares models fitted to the same network; it is
not certain that it is appropriate for choosing the dimension, the random
effects or between a clustered and an unclustered model.

. 
. * --- the BIC for 0, 2, 3 and 4 clusters ---
. nwlsmselect lazega_fr, clusters(0 2 3 4) seed(12)

Selection of the number of latent clusters by BIC (as latentnet's bic.ergmm), ne
> twork lazega_fr
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Clusters         BIC     BIC (Y)     BIC (Z) Mean loglik   BIC - min
------------------------------------------------------------------------
         2    3453.132    3025.173     427.958   -1553.335       0.000  <- best
         3    3460.268    3025.865     434.403   -1553.315       7.136
         0    3467.118    3016.530     450.588   -1551.040      13.986
         4    3467.777    3026.681     441.096   -1553.541      14.646
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sorted by BIC, smaller is better; 0 clusters is the model without clusters.
The BIC compares fits to the same network with the same options.

. matrix list r(table), format(%9.2f)

r(table)[4,8]
       clusters          BIC        BIC_Y        BIC_Z  BIC_effects
r1         0.00      3467.12      3016.53       450.59         0.00
r2         2.00      3453.13      3025.17       427.96         0.00
r3         3.00      3460.27      3025.86       434.40         0.00
r4         4.00      3467.78      3026.68       441.10         0.00

         loglik         used        delta
r1     -1551.04         0.00        13.99
r2     -1553.34         2.00         0.00
r3     -1553.31         3.00         7.14
r4     -1553.54         4.00        14.65

. display "best number of clusters: " r(best)
best number of clusters: 2

. 
. * --- the same comparison with random sender and receiver effects; refit keeps
>  the best model ---
. nwlsmselect lazega_fr, clusters(0 2 3 4) sender receiver seed(12) refit

Selection of the number of latent clusters by BIC (as latentnet's bic.ergmm), ne
> twork lazega_fr
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Clusters         BIC     BIC (Y)     BIC (Z) Mean loglik   BIC - min
------------------------------------------------------------------------
         2    3364.487    2820.765     421.804   -1487.138       0.000  <- best
         3    3364.575    2823.273     419.268   -1487.955       0.088
         4    3367.102    2821.847     422.803   -1487.436       2.615
         0    3379.585    2815.788     441.720   -1486.275      15.098
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sorted by BIC, smaller is better; 0 clusters is the model without clusters.
The BIC compares fits to the same network with the same options.

. estat bic

BIC of the latent position model (as latentnet's bic.ergmm)
